# C2 cb13c86..054fbb3: added and modified files only (deleted files listed, their content omitted)
054fbb3 BrokerProcess owns the control pipe and scans each drive on its own channel

## Commit message
BrokerProcess owns the control pipe and scans each drive on its own channel

BrokerProcess replaces the deleted client: one control pipe per session with
request ids allocated past zero and every retained id, control frames finished
under a process-owned bound once started, and a single control reader that
ends the process loudly. Each scan opens its own drive pipe through the owned
channel-open handshake and reads Cursor, ScanProgress, ScanReady and one
terminal frame; a proven lost catch-up returns the block with its loss, which
BrokerMftBlockProducer copies to MftBlockProduceResult.CatchUpLoss.
BrokerTestHarness runs a host in process over named in-memory pipes.

The host and the client share one frame reader, which rejects a length prefix
that is not positive or exceeds a 1 GiB maximum with InvalidDataException before
allocating. BrokerLiveness declares the liveness limits later tasks enforce.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

